      "math_academy_id": "q-336309",
      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}}.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ Line $\\text{L1}$ identifies ${x}_{2}(t)$ as a column of $Φ(t),$ so ${x}_{2}(t)$ must satisfy the differential equation. In particular,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from the fact that $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix and line $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)],$ the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{differentiating each column}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{factoring out }A\\text{ on the left}.$",
